# Overlay for a board WITH PSRAM - the ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1-N16R8's 8 MB of octal
# PSRAM - for the shapes that run a network:
#
#   SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.psram" idf.py build
#
# WiFi, lwIP, the HTTP client and server, the player and the E-AC-3 decoder do
# not all fit the S3's internal SRAM. Measured on a DevKitC-1 on 2026-09-10 with
# the demo stream (E-AC-3 5.1 with objects, folded to Lo/Ro): even with WiFi's
# IRAM optimisations turned off to give the heap more, 227,852 bytes of internal
# heap were free when the player started, and 31 ms later the next 6,144 bytes
# the decoder asked for failed with 7,656 left. So the larger allocations go to
# PSRAM: plain malloc, and with it every `new` the decoder makes, may use it
# (SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC), and anything of 16 KB or more tries it first
# (SPIRAM_MALLOC_ALWAYSINTERNAL), which keeps the small, hot allocations in
# internal SRAM. The WiFi and lwIP stacks try PSRAM first too, and the player
# puts its ring there.
#
# A decoder with part of its state in PSRAM is slower in bursts. With the render
# and the sink in the decode task, the default 21 ms DMA queue did not ride them
# out: 484 of 12,000 blocks arrived to an empty queue over the demo looped for
# 64 s, and it took a 64 ms queue - twelve descriptors of 256 frames, 24 KB of
# internal SRAM - for none to. Now the render and the sink run in the player's
# output task on core 0 (planning/esp32-714-realtime.md, decisions 1 and 2), fed
# by sixteen decoded blocks - 85 ms - in PSRAM, and that ring rides out the
# bursts. The DMA queue only has to cover the output task being held off by
# WiFi on its own core, so it is back to 21 ms: four descriptors of 256 frames,
# 8 KB.
#
# A local source (partition, fatfs, sd) needs none of this: its decoder, a
# 7.1.4 render included, runs out of internal SRAM.
#
# QEMU cannot emulate S3 PSRAM (espressif/qemu#129), so CI never uses this file.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_80M=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MALLOC_ALWAYSINTERNAL=16384
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y
# Not in the memory test at boot: it takes a second on 8 MB and says nothing
# a player needs to know.
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MEMTEST=n
CONFIG_AC3FORGE_EXAMPLE_OUTPUT_BLOCKS=16
CONFIG_AC3FORGE_EXAMPLE_I2S_DMA_DESCRIPTORS=4
CONFIG_AC3FORGE_EXAMPLE_I2S_DMA_FRAMES=256
